From 6ef763124189055872ed9bf6e22e72c4d82841c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 23:30:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fileset: add `sparse()` function

This adds a `sparse()` fileset function that matches the files within the
current working copy's sparse patterns. It makes it easy to focus on the
sparse checkout, for example `jj log -r 'files(sparse())'` only shows
revisions that touch files in the sparse checkout.

The sparse patterns are loaded by `WorkspaceCommandEnvironment::new()` and
passed to the fileset parser through `FilesetParseContext` (and
`RevsetWorkspaceContext` for `files()` in revsets). Where no sparse patterns
are available, such as in filesets loaded from config, `sparse()` is an
error.

Closes #7816
